 The `pi` segment tags the brand with the active named profile (`π-work`; see [Profiles](config-usage.md#profiles)). Set `statusLine.segmentOptions.pi.showProfile: false` to hide the tag.
 
+The `usage_bar` segment draws a five-cell progress bar and a percent for the active account of the active provider (`━━─── 42%`, or `==--- 42%` with the ASCII symbol set), warning-coloured from 50% and error-coloured from 80%. It shows the most constraining quota window: the 5 Hour window by default, and the 7 Day window, tagged `7d`, when that is more used (daily and monthly windows count too for providers that report them; a tie keeps the 5 Hour window). It reads the same cached usage reports as the `usage` segment, refreshed no more often than every five minutes, and renders nothing when the provider reports no such window. It sits right after `context_pct` in the `default` preset; add `usage_bar` to `statusLine.leftSegments` or `statusLine.rightSegments` with `statusLine.preset: custom` to use it in a custom line.
+
+When a provider holds two or more stored OAuth accounts, the `model` segment names the session's account by its stored position, the order `omp usage accounts` prints (A is the first): `Anthropic (B) > Sonnet 5.5`, and the footer shows the raw id as `anthropic-b/claude-sonnet-5-5`. A provider with one account is unchanged, and model ids themselves are never rewritten.
+
 The `cost` segment shows recorded session costs. For an active provider/model with scheduled pricing, it appends `↑` during peak hours or `↓` off-peak, refreshing at boundaries even while idle. The arrow reflects the current tariff, not past spending; flat-price models and explicit cost overrides have no arrow. See [usage costs and time-based pricing](models.md#usage-costs-and-time-based-pricing) for the UTC schedule and estimation semantics.
 
